  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Literature review and stakeholder consultation, Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aim of the projectLiterature review and stakeholder consultation to establish a shared agenda for addressing the &quot;build, neglect, and rebuild&quot; cycle in the water sector, with a collaborative approach in Bangladesh.This assignment, funded through the Partners for Water Programme by the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO), aims to address the recurring &quot;build, neglect, and rebuild&quot; cycle in Bangladesh&apos;s water sector.The Netherlands, known for its water management expertise, seeks to strengthen its international partnerships through the Netherlands International Water Ambition (IWA). This assignment will be carried out by MetaMeta and the Bangladesh University of Engineering and Technology (BUET).The assignment involves conducting a literature review, stakeholder consultations, comparative analysis, and proposing practical recommendations to break the cycle. Key counterpart organisations include the Government of Bangladesh, private sector entities and civil society groups.The project spans from September 2023 to November 2023, with a strong focus on local collaboration and co-creation.</narrative>
  </description>
